From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilia Alshanetsky <ilia@ilia.ws>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 15/30] Fix compressed block size validation

CompressedInput::Decompress() accepted a declared compressed size below
the 9-byte frame header. The header write grows the buffer to 9 bytes,
but the payload read then asks for `compressed - HEADER_SIZE` bytes,
which wraps to nearly 2^64 in size_t, so the peer can write as many
bytes past the buffer as it sends. Reject sizes below HEADER_SIZE before
allocating, and report the declared size in both size errors. Backport
of upstream commits f0f2927 and 1d60058 (ClickHouse/clickhouse-cpp#566).
---
 clickhouse/base/compressed.cpp | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/clickhouse/base/compressed.cpp b/clickhouse/base/compressed.cpp
--- a/clickhouse/base/compressed.cpp
+++ b/clickhouse/base/compressed.cpp
@@ -79,7 +79,11 @@
     }
 
     if (compressed > DBMS_MAX_COMPRESSED_SIZE) {
-        throw CompressionError("compressed data too big");
+        throw CompressionError("compressed block size " + std::to_string(compressed) + " exceeds maximum allowed, data is likely corrupted");
+    }
+
+    if (compressed < HEADER_SIZE) {
+        throw CompressionError("compressed block size " + std::to_string(compressed) + " is smaller than header, data is likely corrupted");
     }
 
     Buffer tmp(compressed);
